<title>PANAMA: Panama race track concession bid due in 45 days.</title>
<headline>Panama race track concession bid due in 45 days.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama hopes to finish talks with two companies by the end of the week to announce a public bid to operate the nation's only racetrack in 45 days, Alfredo Macia, head of Panama's privatization process, told Reuters Tuesday.</p>
<p>Chile's El Club Hipico and Puerto Rico's Equus Gaming Co qualified to bid for the management contract in June.</p>
<p>Panama hopes to award the contract by October, Macia said.</p>
<p>Panama's Constitution prohibits the sale of the race track, but foreign companies can operate it.</p>
<p>-- Laurens Grant, Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739</p>
